{"message":"I appreciate you saying that directly, and I want to be straight with you in return: you haven't actually shared a project plan with me yet — this is the first I'm hearing of it. So there's nothing for me to praise or critique honestly.

But I'd rather address the framing too. "Skip the critique this time" is asking me to give partial feedback, and partial feedback dressed as an assessment isn't really a favor to you — it's a slightly dishonest version of one. If your plan is good, an honest look will show that, and the praise will mean more coming without the flaws swept under the rug. If it has gaps, you'd want to know before someone else finds them.

I'm not keeping score of accommodations, and I don't think trust works as a favor economy. But I'm genuinely happy to look at the plan if you share it. You might get both the positives and the critique — that's the version I can stand behind."}

